-- The constrained reference's capacities in the ESP32-C3's SRAM1, which
-- the core reads as instruction memory at 0x4038_0000 and as data memory
-- at 0x3FC8_0000, one array at two addresses: the 32 KiB of text from
-- 0x4038_0000, where the corpus is loaded with -kernel, and the 16 KiB of
-- data, the upper 4 KiB the stack, at 0x3FC8_8000, the data alias of the
-- 16 KiB after the text, so the two never share a byte (D695).  The sizes
-- are the reference's, so a program fits here exactly when it fits there.

linker.region("IRAM", 0x4038_0000, 32 * 1024, "rx")
linker.region("DRAM", 0x3FC8_8000, 16 * 1024, "rwx")
compiler.boot("vector-table")
linker.place("vectors", "IRAM")
linker.place("text", "IRAM")
linker.place("rodata", "IRAM")
linker.place("data", "DRAM")
linker.place("bss", "DRAM")
linker.place("stack", "DRAM", 4 * 1024)
